^orange;COMMANDMENT 6^reset;
Thou shall build into thee sky, to get thineself closer to the Cultivator.

^orange;COMMANDMENT 7^reset;
Only thine Chosen Ones are senteth into thee unknown to protecteth other races.
^orange;COMMANDMENT 8^reset;
Outsiders of thine village are notteth welcome. Sendeth thee away.

^cyan;The Cupid^white;
The Cupid is a weak Angel with a small pair of wings. Although Cupids are often associated with love, actual Cupids have nothing to do with it at all. That fact actually surprised me, not gonna lie.

^cyan;The Angel^white;
Your typical Angel, these ones have regular-sized feathery wings.

^cyan;The Cherubim^white;
These Angels have two pairs of wings that sprout from their back.

They are considered stronger than 'regular Angels'.

^cyan;The Ophanim^white;
These odd Angels have two pairs of wings with multiple eyes in them. The eyes help them see a full view of their surroundings.

^cyan;The Serohalaphim^white;
The wings of these Angels are interesting. Behind them floats a giant halo, with 3 pairs of small, unconnected wings. They are remarkable.

^cyan;The Seraphim^white;
The most recognizable type of Angel--with three pairs of mighty wings.

^cyan;The Archangel^white;
One of the most powerful types of Angels out there..the Archangel. Usually, these Angels have a single pair of large, spiky wings.

^cyan;The Ultarubim^white;
These Angels are rumored to have massive wings that are vast and menacing compared to their body.

^cyan;Progressing and Getting New Wings^white;
Although you'd ^green;think that Angels would remain at a single type^green; forever, ^green;they do not^reset;! They can actually "^orange;rank up^reset;", essentially, get new wings, and become more powerful.

The way Angels do this is either by ^green;slaying many Demons, doing many courageous acts, or helping us "Mortals"^reset;. From what I've learned, most passive Angels do not really care about becoming more powerful unless they are a Guard or Guardian.

